    </div>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_sentiment}" alt="Mean Sentiment Polarity by App">
    </div>

    <p><strong>Observation:</strong> While star ratings provide a quick glance at user satisfaction, sentiment polarity captures the nuanced tone of user reviews, highlighting disparities between declared ratings and actual textual sentiment.</p>
</div>

<div class="section" id="thematic-complaint-analysis">
    <h2>3. Thematic Complaint Analysis by Application</h2>
    <p>A regex-derived thematic tagging system categorized reviews into four buckets: General, Pricing, Bugs, and Accuracy. Understanding which specific themes drive negative reviews for each competitor is crucial for strategic positioning.</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_themes}" alt="Review Theme Distribution by App">
    </div>

    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>App</th>
            <th>Bugs (%)</th>
            <th>Accuracy (%)</th>
            <th>Pricing (%)</th>
        </tr>
        {theme_table_rows}
    </table>

    <p><strong>Strategic Implication:</strong> Competitors with high 'Bugs' percentages are vulnerable to stability-focused marketing, while those struggling with 'Accuracy' may lose high-intent professional users.</p>
</div>

<div class="section" id="sentiment-rating-divergence">
    <h2>4. Sentiment-Rating Divergence & Sarcasm Detection</h2>
    <p>A key differentiator in this analysis is identifying "mismatches" where the explicit star rating contradicts the review text's emotional sentiment (e.g., a 1-star review with positive polarity, or a 5-star review with negative polarity, often indicating sarcasm or unresolved feature requests).</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_mismatch}" alt="Sentiment-Rating Mismatch Rate">
    </div>

    <p><strong>Note on Mismatch Definition:</strong> A mismatch is defined as a review with &ge;4 stars and &le;-0.1 polarity, or &le;2 stars and &ge;0.1 polarity. High mismatch rates suggest users are conflicted, possibly retaining the app due to brand loyalty or lack of alternatives despite immediate frustrations.</p>
</div>

<div class="section" id="review-depth-emotion">
    <h2>5. Review Depth & Emotional Intensity</h2>
    <p>Does frustration breed verbosity? We analyzed the correlation between word counts, star ratings, and community engagement (Thumbs Up).</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_depth}" alt="Average Word Count by Star Rating">
    </div>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{img_engagement}" alt="Average Thumbs Up Count by Theme">
    </div>

    <p><strong>Findings:</strong> Displeased users (1-star and 2-star ratings) tend to write longer, more detailed reviews. Furthermore, community engagement (Thumbs Up) spikes on specific thematic complaints, suggesting that critical reviews resonate heavily with the broader user base.</p>
</div>

