    <h2>6. Strategic Recommendations</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Prioritize Stability Over New Features (If 'Bugs' > 15%):</strong> If our app indexes high on bug complaints relative to peers, halt non-essential feature development to address core performance stability.</li>
        <li><strong>Refine the Paywall Experience:</strong> High pricing complaint rates indicate either sticker shock or unclear value propositions. A/B test onboarding flows to better justify premium tiers before prompting for payment.</li>
        <li><strong>Implement Sarcasm/Nuance Detection in Internal Dashboards:</strong> Move beyond simple star-rating averages for internal KPIs. Incorporate sentiment-rating divergence metrics to catch emerging frustrations before they reflect in app store aggregates.</li>
        <li><strong>Address 'Highly Upvoted' Negative Reviews Promptly:</strong> The data shows that specific thematic complaints receive more 'Thumbs Up'. Customer support should prioritize resolving issues raised in long, highly-engaged negative reviews to prevent them from anchoring public perception.</li>
        <li><strong>Capitalize on Competitor Weaknesses:</strong> Target marketing campaigns at the specific vulnerabilities (e.g., "Hallucination-free" or "No hidden paywalls") of our closest competitors based on their highest thematic complaint areas.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

</body>
</html>
